  "limitations": [
    "Source-reported altimetric tracking spans, with table values independently checked against source separation dates and last-trackable dates. These are not verified physical lifetimes.",
    "Tracking contours are adaptive: 30 cm initially, reduced by reported decrements of 10, 5, 3 or 2 cm, typically ending near 8 or 5 cm. Each feature last contour level is unspecified. Tracking required manual assistance during interactions.",
    "Xtra, Juggernaut and Ulysses retain the southern source branch after splitting. The Lifespan column includes their pre-split interval; the separate from-split column is retained only as context. No secondary inherits the parent span.",
    "Source endpoints are labels of separation and last trackability. They do not establish physical birth/death, complete daily sampling, material coherence or a continuous volume history.",
    "Registry initial dates and month-resolution dissipation labels remain separate from this source. Name/date context is not a verified physical registry crosswalk.",
    "No volume, width, depth, state geometry, annual envelope or ranking is inferred. The U2 conflict remains unresolved."
  ],
